1 THEN

   Introduces what an IF runs when its expression is true: the command
   after it on the IF's line, or, in an IF block, the commands from
   THEN to the block's ELSE or ENDIF.  A block's THEN must be the
   command after the IF.

   Format

     IF expression THEN [$] command
     THEN [[$] command]

   It leaves $STATUS as it was.  See IF.
